        "original_id": "1f036595-bb76-549e-8274-f43ef5704c73",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Annette Snell\n- Events: Southern Airways Flight 242 crash\n- Products: Southern Airways Flight 242, DC-9-31 jet\n- Places: New Hope, Paulding County, Georgia, United States\n\nFacts:\n- On April 4, 1977, Southern Airways Flight 242, a DC-9-31 jet registered N1335U, made a forced landing on a highway in New Hope, Paulding County, Georgia, United States.\n- On April 4, 1977, Southern Airways Flight 242 suffered hail damage in a severe thunderstorm and lost thrust on both engines.\n- Annette Snell died in the Southern Airways Flight 242 crash.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
